Z||000000||overlord||03-20-2000||09:54 AM||||where should i hook up the power tomy new amplifier?     fuse box?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Monkeyman||03-20-2000||10:04 AM||||Not the fuse box!!  Hook it up directly to the battery.  If you remove the ECM and it's bracket, there is a rubber disc behind it on the firewall.  You can cut a small hole it that and run your power cable through that directly into the engine bay.  (If you didn't know about this, don't feel bad.  I just found out about a week ago!)  Most stereo stores sell an adapter that goes on your battery terminal that you can hook your amp to.||||reg||1
Z||000002||overlord||03-20-2000||10:47 AM||||alrighty...thankyou sir.||||reg||1
Z||000003||batboy||03-20-2000||10:50 AM||||An amp should have a separate power wire from the battery and it should have a in-line fuse too.||||reg||1
Z||000004||phillip||03-20-2000||12:58 PM||||didn't one of you two(bat or monkey) move your battery to the front?where is your amp and how did you reroute power? mine is in the front trunk but i only used 8 guage cable. it runs inside the car from front to back. if i can get a 4 guage  through the same area wiil it be big enough to supply power for the car? that way i could just kind of swap power wires. also for such a long power run,did you feel a need to fuse the lead like you would a stereo amp?||||reg||1
